  "response": "I’m using the repository’s `crimes-codebase-risk` workflow to ground the proposal in the actual four JSX subtrees, then I’ll define the smallest shared API that preserves create/edit differences.\n\nFinding `crime_00071` identifies the repeated footer `<div>` in four invoice forms: the action row containing the Cancel link and submit button.\n\nProposed component: `InvoiceFormActions`\n\n```tsx\ntype InvoiceFormActionsProps = {\n  cancelHref?: string;        // defaults to \"/dashboard/invoices\"\n  cancelLabel?: ReactNode;    // defaults to \"Cancel\"\n  children: ReactNode;        // primary-action slot\n};\n```\n\n```tsx\nexport function InvoiceFormActions({\n  cancelHref = \"/dashboard/invoices\",\n  cancelLabel = \"Cancel\",\n  children,\n}: InvoiceFormActionsProps) {\n  return (\n    <div className=\"mt-6 flex justify-end gap-4\">\n      <Link href={cancelHref} className=\"...\">\n        {cancelLabel}\n      </Link>\n      {children}\n    </div>\n  );\n}\n```\n\nUsage:\n\n```tsx\n<InvoiceFormActions>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Create Invoice</Button>\n</InvoiceFormActions>\n```\n\n```tsx\n<InvoiceFormActions>\n  <Button type=\"submit\">Edit Invoice</Button>\n</InvoiceFormActions>\n```\n\nThe `children` slot keeps the component compatible with future pending-state or specialized submit buttons without adding form-specific behavior to the layout component. An optional `leadingActions?: ReactNode` slot could be added later, but it is unnecessary for the current four callers.\n\nFiles to modify:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/create-form.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/edit-form.tsx`\n\nBecause `final-example` and `starter-example` are independent Next.js applications, each should add its own:\n\n- `dashboard/final-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n- `dashboard/starter-example/app/ui/invoices/form-actions.tsx`\n\nThat avoids coupling two tutorial snapshots while ensuring create/edit forms within each application cannot drift. If these applications are later converted into a workspace, the same API can move unchanged into a shared UI package.",
